"about.body" = "■ ABOUT
A native macOS image viewer: instant opening, buttery folder navigation, gesture zoom and EXIF at a glance. Fully on-device — no network requests, no data collection, no accounts.

■ HOW TO USE
Drop a folder or image into the window to browse; or right-click an image in Finder and open it with PixDeck.
← → to flip; scroll / pinch / ↑↓ to zoom; drag to pan; double-click toggles fit ⇄ 100%; Esc resets.
R / L rotate the view; ⌘⌥S writes the rotation back to the file losslessly; Return renames; ⌘⌫ moves to Trash.
⌘S exports a compressed copy (location / format / quality); the Tools menu adds batch convert and batch rename.
S starts a slideshow; I shows photo info; T toggles the thumbnail strip; F for full screen. Controls auto-hide after a few idle seconds and reappear on mouse movement.
The interface and every message follow your system language automatically (14 supported).";
"about.shortcutsTitle" = "Keyboard Shortcuts";
"sc.title" = "Keyboard Shortcuts";
"sc.body" = "← / →  Previous / Next (wraps around)
↑ / ↓  Zoom in / out (hold to repeat)
R / L  Rotate 90° CW / CCW
S  Slideshow (3s per photo, S to stop)
Space  Preview fitted to the image (press again to exit)
Double-click  Fit ⇄ 100%
Esc  Back to fit (exits full screen first)
1 / 0  Actual size / Fit to window
Pinch / scroll  Zoom at cursor, drag or ⌘+scroll to pan
View › Scroll Wheel  switch to paging through photos
I  Photo info    T  Thumbnail strip    F  Full screen
⌘⇧C  Batch convert    ⌘⇧B  Batch rename    ⌘⇧D  Set wallpaper
⌘⇧K  Cleanup Mode Beta: duplicates, closed eyes, blur
⌘S  Quick export    ⌘⇧E  Export as…
Return  Rename current image
⌘⌥S  Save rotation to file
⌘⌫  Move to trash    ⌘R  Reveal in Finder
Drop a folder or image to open";

